  "origin": "OSCAR v21.09 is derived from the Common Crawl snapshot of February 2021. Common Crawl publishes web crawl data under permissive terms; OSCAR processes it into language-separated, cleaned corpora. BigScience selected OSCAR v21.09 to make up the remaining 38% of ROOTS (after the 62% from crowdsourced catalogue sources), motivated by the need to include web-crawl data for comparability with other large LM training corpora. BigScience applied extensive human-curated filters (documented in Appendix C of the ROOTS paper) to remove repetitive content, pornographic/spam text, machine-generated SEO content, and personally identifiable information. The license field carries CC-BY-4.0 as the Common Crawl terms-of-use convention, but the underlying web pages are individually under heterogeneous licenses (the per-document multi-license aggregate problem, as in the Pleias OpenSource record) — this is a representative IRI, not a faithful per-document license. See notes/stress-test-bloom-roots.md (Gap B discussion). ROOTS was released as a gated subset subject to committing to the BigScience ethical charter (https://hf.co/spaces/bigscience/ethical-charter).",
